<title>MALAYSIA: Ringgit eases in London on U.S. funds selling.</title>
<headline>Ringgit eases in London on U.S. funds selling.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ringgit retreated sharply on selling by U.S. funds in the thin London market, dealers in Singapore and London said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said many funds were still short dollar and were covering their positions, but volumes remained low.</p>
<p>At 1040 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.5145/55 a dollar against a high of 2.5070 in the morning.</p>
<p>&quot;After dollar/ringgit failed to break below 2.5070 a dollar, the selling pressure continued building,&quot; said a dealer with a U.S. bank in London.</p>
</text>
